```csharp
using System;

namespace PalindromeChecker
{
    class Program
    {
        static void Main(string[] args)
        {
            Console.Write("Enter a string: ");
            string input = Console.ReadLine();
            bool isPalindrome = IsPalindrome(input);

            if (isPalindrome)
            {
                Console.WriteLine("The given string is a palindrome.");
            }
            else
            {
                Console.WriteLine("The given string is NOT a palindrome.");
            }
        }

        static bool IsPalindrome(string s)
        {
            string sCleaned = CleanString(s);
            int length = sCleaned.Length;
            for (int i = 0; i < length / 2; i++)
            {
                if (sCleaned[i] != sCleaned[length - i - 1])
                {
                    return false;
                }
            }
            return true;
        }

        static string CleanString(string s)
        {
            return s.Replace(" ", "").ToLower();
        }
    }
}
```

## Explanation

This program contains a 'Main' method that takes user input, checks if the given string is a palindrome using the 'IsPalindrome' method, and then displays the result.

### IsPalindrome Method

This method takes a string as input and returns a boolean value that represents whether the string is a palindrome or not. 

It first removes any whitespace and converts the string to lowercase using the 'CleanString' method. Then, it loops through the string up to its midpoint, comparing an equal number of characters from each end. If any pair of characters doesn't match, it returns 'false' immediately, indicating that the string isn't a palindrome. If the loop completes without finding any mismatched characters, it returns 'true'.

### CleanString Method

This method removes whitespaces and converts the string to lowercase. Whitespaces are removed by using Replace method andToLower method is used to convert the string to lowercase.

## Edge Cases

1. **Special characters**: This program doesn't take account of special characters and considers them as part of the string when determining whether it's a palindrome. Depending on your requirements, you may want to remove special characters or treat them in a specific way.

2. **Case sensitivity**: This program ignores the case. For example, "Aba" will be considered a palindrome since it's case insensitive. If you need to consider the case, remove the 'ToLower()' function call in the 'CleanString' method.

