Two sets are considered disjoint if they have no elements in common. In this case:

A = {3, 5, 7}
B = {4, 6, 8}

These two sets do not share any elements, so they are indeed disjoint. 

Now you might be curious about what other types of relationships exist between sets. Apart from disjoint, there are also subsets and supersets. If all elements of one set are contained within another set, then the former is called a subset, and the latter is called a superset. For example, if we have sets C = {3, 5} and D = {1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6}, we can say that C is a subset of D, and D is a superset of C.

To animate an element when it comes into the viewport using CSS, we will use scrolling events with JavaScript to trigger CSS animations._following these steps:

1. Create your HTML structure
```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
