I can help you design a GraphQL server acting as a BFF layer between the REST API you mentioned and a front-end application using React and Flutter. Here's a step-by-step guide on how to do that:

1. Set up a new Node.js project for the GraphQL server:
   ```
   mkdir piecejobs-graphql
   cd piecejobs-graphql
   npm init -y
   ```

2. Install the necessary dependencies:
   ```
   npm install express express-graphql graphql graphql-playground-middleware-express axios
   ```

3. Create an index.js file to write the GraphQL server code:
   ```
   touch index.js
   ```

4. Import the necessary dependencies and set up an express server in index.js:
   ```javascript
   const express = require('express');
   const graphqlHTTP = require('express-graphql');
   const { buildSchema } = require('graphql');
   const expressPlayground = require('graphql-playground-middleware-express').default;
   const axios = require('axios');

   const app = express();
   ```

5. Define GraphQL schema for the available endpoints:
   ```javascript
   const schema = buildSchema(`
     type Job {
       id: ID!
       title: String
       description: String
       location: String
       created_at: String
     }

     input JobInput {
       title: String
       description: String
       location: String
     }

     type Query {
       jobs: [Job]
     }

     type Mutation {
       createJob(input: JobInput): Job
     }
   `);
   ```

6. Define the resolvers to fetch data from the REST API:
   ```javascript
   const API_BASE_URL = 'http://quickshyft.co.za/api/v1';

   const root = {
     jobs: async () => {
       const response = await axios.get(`${API_BASE_URL}/jobs`);
       return response.data;
     },
     createJob: async ({ input }) => {
       const response = await axios.post(`${API_BASE_URL}/jobs`, input);
       return response.data;
     },
   };
   ```

7. Set up the GraphQL server with schema and root enpoints, and add the playground middleware:
   ```javascript
   app.use(
     '/graphql',
     graphqlHTTP({
       schema: schema,
       rootValue: root,
       graphiql: false,
     }),
   );

   app.get('/playground', expressPlayground({ endpoint: '/graphql' }));

   const PORT = process.env.PORT || 4000;

   app.listen(PORT, () => {
     console.log(`Listening on http://localhost:${PORT}`);
   });
   ```

