3. **TemplateEngine.Docx**: This library allows you to use existing Word document templates to generate new Word documents with placeholders. You specify the template, define the data to replace the placeholders, and the library takes care of filling in the data for you.

GitHub: https://github.com/antonmaju/TemplateEngine.Docx
NuGet: https://www.nuget.org/packages/TemplateEngine.Docx

Here's a simple example using TemplateEngine.Docx:

```csharp
using TemplateEngine.Docx;

// Load the template document
using (var template = new TemplateProcessor("Template.docx"))
{
    // Replace placeholders with data
    template.FillContent(new Content(
        new FieldContent("FirstName", "John"),
        new FieldContent("LastName", "Doe"),
        new FieldContent("Email", "johndoe@example.com")
    ));

    // Save the generated document
    template.SaveChanges("Output.docx");
}
```

